      "detail": "\n\nBoth files are updated. Here's the summary of changes:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### `genome/AGENTS.md`\nAdded 5 specific guidelines derived from observed failures in `evidence.json`:\n\n1. **PowerShell-native commands only** \u2014 Evidence shows agents repeatedly used `ls -la`, `Find-Item`, and `cat << 'EOF'` in Windows PowerShell, all failing with \"command not recognized\" or syntax errors. The fix was to use `Get-ChildItem -Recurse`, `type`, `Set-Content`.\n\n2. **Read file before patching** \u2014 Evidence shows agents attempting `apply_patch` with incorrect context multiple times before reading the file with `Get-Content` to get exact line numbers.\n\n3. **Check existing code before implementing** \u2014 Agents sometimes started from scratch when a class skeleton already existed, wasting effort.\n\n4. **School class cross-grade duplicate bug** \u2014 Evidence shows `add_student` allowed the same student in multiple grades, violating the requirement that each student appears at most once across the entire roster. The fix: check ALL grades, not just the target grade.\n\n5. **Don't repeat failing command patterns** \u2014 When a command fails, try the PowerShell equivalent instead of repeating the same failing pattern.\n\n### `genome/meta/IMPROVE.md`\nAdded a dated record of the changes with the evidence that supports each one.\n\nAll rules are specific to the observed failure mechanisms and applicable across tasks in this Windows PowerShell environment."
